ances electromagnetic performance and thermal constraints. The proposed framework, termed MPOSM-TD3, is experimentally validated to simultaneously reduce the maximum winding temperature by 15.3\textasciicircumi̧rc \textC and improve operational efficiency by 0.94%.},
 author = {Wang, Chen and Dong, Tianyu and Zhu, Guixiang and Nan, Yue and Zhang, Zhuoran},
 date = {2026-04},
 doi = {10.1109/TII.2025.3644943},
 issn = {1941-0050},
 journaltitle = {IEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics},
 keywords = {/unread, Analytical models, Couplings, Deep reinforcement learning (DRL), Density measurement, Electromagnetics, high-speed permanent magnet (HSPM) machine, Integrated circuit modeling, interpretability analysis, light gradient boosting machine (LightGBM), Multiphysics, multiphysics field optimization, Optimization, Permanent magnets, Power system measurements, Stator windings},
 number = {4},
 pages = {2699--2709},
 title = {Interpretable Multiphysics Field Optimization Approach for HSPM Machine Based on Deep Reinforcement Learning},
